{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Partners and Tornado appeal because polished duets and vocal harmonies connect with my interest in ensemble singing on A Musical Affair and Lead With Your Heart.",
    "Blown Away feels like a plausible next choice because expressive singing and polished country production connect my enjoyment of vocal performances with 747 and Golden."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Loaded and Garth Brooks: The Ultimate Hits lean toward broad country retrospectives, while today I am more drawn to vocal interplay or relaxing orchestral listening.",
    "I Am and Album Number Two give me too little recognizable connection to my listening interests, and I would need to know the performer before choosing The Classic Christmas Album."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in 747 and Golden seems to have been taken as a broad appetite for country music, although harmonies and the character of the singing matter more to me than that shared label.",
    "A Christmas title connects with Christmas At Downton Abbey only partly; the performers and musical atmosphere determine whether I actually want to hear it."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My most recent choice was relaxing classical music, and I miss recommendations that would continue that calm, orchestral mood.",
    "My listening also includes theatrical vocals and Downton Abbey music, so I would welcome more choices connected by expressive ensemble singing and orchestral arrangements."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The choices recognize my country listening but give too little weight to the vocal harmonies, theatrical singing, and relaxing orchestral mood that guide my choices today."
}"}
